WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.101
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:03.269
We're here with Hillary and
Chelsea Clinton.

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.138
I don't want to miss the
opportunity to ask you

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:07.273
about some things in the news.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.342
With the Dobbs decision --
-Mm.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:13.213
-I think in the days after,
it seemed like -- maybe this is

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.682
the risk you put yourself at
when you take a snapshot

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.483
of a very small period of time.
It seemed like people were

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:19.152
saying that Democrats were
caught very flat-footed,

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:22.021
like they weren't expecting it.
But in the months since, it does

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:24.557
seem like Republicans are
scrambling, especially ones

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:25.858
that have won primaries
who are now trying to

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:27.594
back off their decision.

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:28.761
We have a lot of Republicans

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:30.697
saying it should be decided by
the states.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:32.164
We have Lindsey Graham then
coming forward

00:00:32.164 --> 00:00:34.366
and saying there should be
a federal ban.

00:00:34.366 --> 00:00:37.337
Do you feel like this is, you
know, an opportunity, obviously

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.839
one that came at a great cost of
this decision?

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:44.143
But, you know, as the midterms
approach, how do you feel this

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:48.448
is going to, I don't know, move
voters one way or the other?

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:52.085
-Well, I can only say based on
what we've seen so far,

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:56.422
it seems to have encouraged
a huge number

00:00:56.422 --> 00:01:00.059
of women and young people
to register to vote.

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:02.195
The numbers
from across the country are...

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:06.298
[ Cheers and applause ]
...higher than I've seen

00:01:06.298 --> 00:01:07.600
in a very long time.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.435
We also have three elections --

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:11.270
a special election in New York,

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:14.907
the Kansas election on the issue
of choice and abortion,

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:17.710
and then the congressional
election Alaska.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:21.213
And in each case,
the pro-choice position won.

00:01:21.213 --> 00:01:24.984
And I think that's a pretty good
snapshot because obviously,

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:27.286
it went literally
across the country.

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:32.991
So look, I think that the
Republicans have been scrambling

00:01:32.991 --> 00:01:36.896
only because they can't quite
believe the blowback.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:40.032
I mean, it's one thing to say
for years,

00:01:40.032 --> 00:01:41.467
"We're going to do this,
we're going to do that,"

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:44.203
and people not take you
seriously because who would have

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:47.306
ever thought that women's rights
would be rolled back?

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:49.008
And that's --
-We did.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:52.011
-Well, you and I did.
But that's because we take

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:54.848
these people at their word
because we know that they are

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:58.250
part of a relentless movement to
literally turn the clock back

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:02.088
on not just women,
but gay rights to enhance

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:07.360
all kinds of, you know, power
for corporations and others,

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.995
and limit individual freedom.

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:13.399
So, if people take seriously
what the court did,

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:17.236
what is happening in states, and
what Lindsey Graham just did,

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:19.172
which was to really
spill the beans --

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:21.107
"we're going to put in
a national --"

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:23.910
-15-week abortion ban.
-Yeah, a ban no matter what you

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.745
might do in your state, then
they should turn out and vote

00:02:26.745 --> 00:02:30.450
and vote for people who, you
know, want to really protect

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:33.620
the right of people to make
their own decisions,

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.321
whatever that decision might be.

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.089
That's what
they're fighting for.

00:02:37.089 --> 00:02:42.661
[ Cheers and applause ]
-And I think, Seth, that to be

00:02:42.661 --> 00:02:45.398
a woman right now is to be
political because politicians

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:48.000
have decided that they know
better what we should do

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.569
with our bodies than we do.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:54.407
-And I think that women and,
thankfully, the men who believe

00:02:54.407 --> 00:03:00.046
that women should have agency
over our lives and ourselves

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:04.951
don't want to go back to a time
where it's actually politicians

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:08.120
and not women and their doctors
making choices.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.489
-Mm-hmm. Absolutely.
-Intimate choices.

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:12.991
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:12.991 --> 00:03:14.927
-I'd be remiss if I didn't ask
you about this.

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:16.428
I don't know if you've noticed
in the news,

00:03:16.428 --> 00:03:20.032
but there's been an issue about
handling classified materials.

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:21.600
-Oh, I heard about that.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:25.838
-We've had some fun here because
we can't help but find

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:28.741
a certain level of hypocrisy
from certain people,

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:32.378
including the fella who handled
this classified material,

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:35.414
because back in the day --
-Oh, so long ago.

00:03:35.414 --> 00:03:38.818
-Yeah, so long ago. I don't know
if you've ever heard this.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.119
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:41.820
He thought
you should be arrested.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.889
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:46.326
And, you know, let me start
by saying

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:48.895
just for the history books,

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:52.799
do you know how many
classified documents I had?

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:55.568
Zero. Zero.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:57.603
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:57.603 --> 00:03:59.472
You know,
you can't make this up.

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:04.177
I mean, the lies they told,
you know, heated rhetoric,

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:06.178
"lock her up,"
all that nonsense,

00:04:06.178 --> 00:04:09.348
it was totally political,
divorced from reality.

00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:15.488
Now we have a serious problem
because if you just read,

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:17.456
and I don't have
any inside information,

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:19.292
what is being found,

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:24.630
nuclear information about
an ally or an adversary.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:28.668
Incredibly top secret --
the kind of stuff, Seth, that

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:32.105
when I was Secretary of State,
when they talk about secret,

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:34.873
top secret, and then special
compartmentalized

00:04:34.873 --> 00:04:38.210
and all of that, sometimes --
usually it was a man.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:43.616
Usually a military officer,
would come into my office

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:48.854
and would have a handcuff that
was attached to a suitcase

00:04:48.854 --> 00:04:51.657
in order to show me something
that was so secret,

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:55.461
he literally had to have it
tied to his hand.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:58.564
And so, it was locked.
And then he would open it.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:01.033
I would read it.
I would sign that I'd read it.

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:02.335
And he would take it back.

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:06.238
That's what some of those
folders on the outside say

00:05:06.238 --> 00:05:07.940
was the kind of information
in it.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:11.076
And so, I don't care what
political party you are,

00:05:11.076 --> 00:05:13.078
but come on, cut the hypocrisy.

00:05:13.078 --> 00:05:15.280
This is a threat
to our national security.

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:20.419
Somebody would actually have in
his country club storage room

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:24.490
his desk, his bedroom,
top secret information.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.158
And you have to ask yourself
"Why?

00:05:26.158 --> 00:05:28.628
What was he going to do with it?
Who was he giving it to?"

00:05:28.628 --> 00:05:31.063
-Or "What had he already done
with it?"

00:05:31.063 --> 00:05:33.633
-And so, let the investigation
go forward

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:35.768
and let's, you know,
find the facts.

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:38.204
Unlike those guys,
I'm not saying "lock him up."

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:39.772
I'm saying
let's just find the facts

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.674
and follow the evidence
wherever it goes.

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:42.808
-Well, I think if he --

00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:46.445
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:49.348
I think if he realizes
he did something wrong,

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:51.451
he'll probably turn himself in
and say "lock me up."

00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:53.085
[ Laughter ]
-Right.

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:55.321
-If I know the man.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:56.956
-He'd want to take
responsibility.

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:58.124
-He will take responsibility,

00:05:58.124 --> 00:05:59.859
if there's one thing we know
about the man.

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:01.660
Hey, Chelsea,
this is very exciting.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:05.397
Especially as someone with three
kids of my own, you wrote a book

00:06:05.397 --> 00:06:07.734
inspired by having
three of yours.

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:09.935
-I did, I did. So, I wrote,
"Welcome to the Big Kids Club"

00:06:09.935 --> 00:06:12.371
because when I was pregnant with
our third, Jasper,

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:14.039
Charlotte and Aidan
had all these questions

00:06:14.039 --> 00:06:16.642
like, you know -- Well, first
they asked, "Is it going to be

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:18.477
a boy or girl?" And I said, "I
don't actually know the answer

00:06:18.477 --> 00:06:19.745
to that because we're going to
be surprised."

00:06:19.745 --> 00:06:21.247
But then they asked other
questions like,

00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:23.549
"When will the baby
talk and walk?"

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:26.652
And "Will the baby poop,
like, on day one?"

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:28.688
And "Why don't babies
have teeth?"

00:06:28.688 --> 00:06:30.623
Because it would really hurt
if you're breastfeeding.

00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:32.291
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:34.293
That's actually not the answer,
totally, but...

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:38.197
[ Laughter ]
So I decided to write a book

00:06:38.197 --> 00:06:39.699
because I thought,
"Well, if we're having

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:42.001
these conversations, we're
probably not the only family

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:45.271
having these conversations."
And so, I wish I had had

00:06:45.271 --> 00:06:47.640
this book when I was pregnant
with Jasper,

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.041
and I was so thankful to Tania

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:51.309
for the extraordinarily
beautiful illustrations.

00:06:51.309 --> 00:06:53.579
And just so proud and excited
it's out in the world.

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:56.014
-Yeah, yeah.
-Well, it's very exciting.

00:06:56.014 --> 00:06:57.883
Thank you both
for making the time.

00:06:57.883 --> 00:06:59.285
It's always a pleasure...
-Thank you, Seth. Thank you.

00:06:59.285 --> 00:07:00.920
-...to see you especially
together.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.688
Hillary and Chelsea Clinton
everybody.

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:05.224
"Gutsy" is now streaming on
Apple TV+.

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:08.027
We'll be right back with
Kate Berlant, everyone.

